 but barely holding on. No shield remains, no whole planet remains, only debris and dust; Aevos stands untouched, overwhelmingly powerful. Preserve readable spatial cause and effect and the detailed painted cosmic style. No gore, additional people, duplicated limbs, face changes, dialogue, subtitles, lettering or logos. Sound: immense low rumble, accelerating air, crushing planetary impact, rocky fragmentation, a clear glasslike shield-break after the first blast, and a final rolling shockwave. No speech or music. Very slow cinematic push toward the shield until impact, then a small physical camera jolt on each of the TWO separate blasts. Stay behind the heroes."
